<description>&lt;p&gt;Mexican special forces captured the cartel leader known as El Chapo Isidro in northern Sinaloa, killing eleven people and setting vehicles ablaze on a highway. Soldiers were attacked during the raid, and the operation sparked a burst of violence that interrupted a local baseball match. The capture was aided by U.S. surveillance drones and intelligence, allowing the raid to proceed without agents on site. The incident occurs amid a broader asymmetric struggle between the Mexican government and drug trafficking syndicates. 37 battle-related deaths were recorded in 1996, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxQdnIxT1p6ZGRtTS1kSFRsc29RcFRqeTFkUlBHMHdZVjNPNHhzVEZYajI4bmtVZ2VETWJtLWZ2XzBNTUNYT0Q4U1A4OUJaclFsWUpzU1BHNzJIWmhoZmZfLVg3dDVxdEFCRkZwTkQ2bDM0SFNBUEpReks2Q3hIWm9WTGEyNGtWcHRaRWhtdU1xazFpNk1rVkhXR2o0MldzZmFwRm5lQy1RRnNtQTR3al9GZ2RKOFU?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxOZkJJbk5kX3ZDU3MyZnp0b3M5UXl1MUllbkpsSkY5eS00TWlwXzhtLXNMSkVNakRDM1ZUMUY0VWFjYVh3Z21DNmg0ekRjakY2TFk2WXNZd09WaVFScW13c0tINVNvNWJqNGJVUGJUbGYxSUF6UzAxdEN4dDdsWXR1eTBwWUJXdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxQNHRIZ1MwYl91TUhrT1c1bS1iS21Ub3JXR1A0elYxZ0NMdVRWci1OVFRqWndlbk9zdC1OVUVSZTdJTmxCZXFyLVczX1h3WURtdnlTZzhNVTNFMWFRNHJmSUZnUkRldE9aRUNaU2w1ZDBXckt2RWg4eElEWERIbVg1RmtlM0dEc1E1QXRkcXhubVhUS3l2dGZlRFV0SkdMR080T2JIX0dWc2kwakZ1YlQwc1B6LWg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxOcFhhdWNpOF9ZYWYwZnZxZnJIOTV4SWVSZnUzeVo2a1hOZlhDRnowc0VrMDBmYndzWVM2OVZJQktzaG95SGpSSlZoV0NkN2k4YlNQNEtiMzVBRHhxMERWeVpNVlNxSmMyQUNnZmZPS1V6RFR6UlpEUWNITGI0NjEtODB5ZURMNmQxM0doQllKUXNoOW1YZ1U2OTFZU0N1c2NqMWtyej